# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large external / derived data — NEVER commit.
#
# data/cache holds ~9.6 GB of downloaded reference data and derived intermediates.
# Thirteen of those files exceed GitHub's 100 MB HARD limit, so committing them
# would get the push rejected outright. All of it is re-fetchable:
#
#     bash scripts/fetch_sumstats.sh
#
# Ignoring data/cache takes the repo from ~9.6 GB to ~9 MB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/cache/*

# ...but DO keep the tiny cached cis-instrument sets (a few KB each). These pin the
# EXACT instruments that produced the L6/L4b/L4c estimates, so results stay
# reproducible even if OpenGWAS drifts or a token expires.
!data/cache/instr_*.rds

# Explicit belt-and-braces for the biggest offenders (covered by data/cache/* above,
# listed so the intent is obvious to a reader):
data/cache/sumstats/
data/cache/*.bed
data/cache/*.bim
data/cache/*.fam
data/cache/1kg.v3.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit the OpenGWAS JWT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Renviron
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quarto / knitr scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.quarto/
*_cache/

# NOTE: rendered *.html and their *_files/ asset directories ARE tracked on purpose —
# they are small (<1 MB total) and let the analyses be read on GitHub without a rerun.
# If you would rather keep the repo source-only, uncomment:
# *.html
# *_files/
# *.html.md
